  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully added the `lateFee` function to `src/reports.js` with comprehensive tests. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n**`src/reports.js` - `lateFee` function**\n- Calculates late fees on overdue invoices\n- Rate: 0.04% of the amount due per day overdue\n- Returns 0 if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n- Calculates daysOverdue using the same logic as `overdueInvoices`\n- Uses `invoiceTotals` to get the amount due (includes VAT, discounts, vouchers)\n- Rounds to nearest cent using `roundCents`\n\n**`test/reports.test.js` - 19 comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Not overdue: returns 0\n- Due date equals asOf: returns 0\n- Simple 1 day overdue: 0.04% of amount\n- Multiple days overdue (10, 100+ days)\n- Amounts with VAT included\n- Amounts with discounts applied\n- Amounts with vouchers applied\n- Multiple lines\n- Zero amount due\n- Small and large amounts\n- Proper rounding to nearest cent\n- Input immutability\n- Non-negative return values\n- Exact rate verification (0.04% per day)\n\n**Test results:** All 293 tests pass (255 original + 38 new tests for vatSummary and lateFee combined).\n\nThe `src/reports.js` module now contains three complete reporting functions:\n1. `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` - identifies overdue invoices\n2. `vatSummary(invoices)` - aggregates VAT by rate\n3. `lateFee(invoice, asOf)` - calculates late fees\n\nAll ready to commit!",
